 Operation: Filter and Extract

Explanation: The operation will filter out the unnecessary information from each row and extract only the dish names. This will make the 'name' column more accurate, complete, and concise.

Here is an example of how to perform this operation using Python:

```python
import re

# Sample data
data = [
    "| __claret_orangeade__",
    "| --EISCHAUM-NOCKEN--",
    "| --JOHANNISBERG-CLAUSS-'86--",
    "| __roast_spring_lamb,_mint_sauce_(ready)__",
    "| COLD_LOBSTER,_MAYONNAISE_SAUCE,_HALF",
    "| veal_cutlet_broiled,_fried_or_breaded",
    "| __beef_pepper_steak_served_with_vegetable,_salad,_roll,_and_choice_of_potato_or_rice__",
    "| --chicken-saute-chasseur,-white-wine-sauce,-parslty-potato-and-green-peas--",
    "| __sweetbread,_tzarine__",
    "| --tomatoes-or-cucumbers-and-lettuce--",
    "| __sea_food_a_la_miramar__",
    "| __MEXICAN_TAMALES__",
    "| fried_ham_and_one_fried_egg",
    "| __?_london_broil_on_toast,_tomato_sauce__",
    "| INDIVIDUAL_WEDDING_CAKES_FOR_EVERYBODY",
    "| --BUTTER-SERVED-FREE-WITH-ORDERS-AMOUNTING-TO-40C--",
    "| vol_au_vent_of_chicken,_fresh_string_beans,_straw_potatoes,_choice_of_salad_or_dessert,_coffee_or_tea",
    "| __?_london_broil_on_toast,_tomato_sauce__",
    "| BROILED_FRESH_POMPANO_FILET_IN_LEMON_BUTTER",
    "| wehlener_rosenberg,_1907,_1/2_bottle,_bottle",
    "| new_beets_fines_herbes",
    "| madère",
    "| ROAST_TAME_DUCK_&_JELLY",
    "| __veal_cutlet_broiled,_fried_or_breaded__",
    "| --veal-cutlet-breaded,-tomato--",
    "| __vol_au_vent_of_chicken,_fresh_string_beans,_straw_potatoes,_choice_of_salad_or_dessert,_coffee_or_tea__",
    "| __vol_au_vent_of_chicken,_fresh_string_beans,_straw_potatoes,_choice_of_salad_or_dessert,_coffee_or_tea__",
    "| __unjointed_fried_half_spring_chicken_on_toast,_country_gravy__",
    "| __schildkrotensuppe_echt,_"lacroix"__"
]

# Regular expression pattern to extract dish names from each row
pattern = re.compile(r'__(\w+[\s\w]+)__|\s*--(\w+[\s\w]+)--')

# Apply the regular expression pattern to each row and extract the dish names
dish_names = [match[1] if match else None for match in map(pattern.findall, data)]

print(dish_names)
```

